@L@LukasVonQis isn’t a hot take….its an obvious logical conclusion.

I have invested, but I am having second thoughts now. Particularly with pensions. I think it might be better to have more short term financial resilience.
But either way I think to just blanket assume a 5% (or more) return year on year will become fundamentally, and permanently wrong, and that should probably be mentioned as a possibility at this stage. Particularly when people are REALLY going to need good financial advice!
